act-preserve-signaled: preserveSignaled is CLEAR on TPM Reset/Restart and
a copy of signaled on TPM Resume

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

TPM 2.0 Part 2, TPMA_ACT: "On a TPM Reset or Restart, preservedSignaled is
CLEAR for all ACT. On a TPM Resume, the state of each ACT signaled is copied
to the corresponding preservedSignaled." ActStartup() instead clears
go.preservedSignaled only after a power loss and otherwise ORs go.signaledACT
into it for every startup type: after a _TPM_Init without power loss, TPM
Reset and TPM Restart keep a stale preserveSignaled (and a TPM Restart after
TPM2_Shutdown(TPM_SU_STATE) sets it), TPM Resume keeps bits of ACTs that no
longer signal, and a TPM Resume after a power loss clears preserveSignaled
(signaled itself is restored by _ActResume()). The fix sets go.preservedSignaled from go.signaledACT (saved by
TPM2_Shutdown(TPM_SU_STATE)) on TPM Resume and clears it otherwise, as tpm-rs
does (tpm2-impl src/act.rs, ActState::startup).

diff --git a/src/ACT_spt.c b/src/ACT_spt.c
index ed50bfb..4a50fd0 100644
--- a/src/ACT_spt.c
+++ b/src/ACT_spt.c
@@ -101,10 +101,13 @@ BOOL ActStartup(STARTUP_TYPE type)
     
     // If this not a cold start, copy all the current 'signaled' settings to
     // 'preservedSignaled'.
-    if(g_powerWasLost)
-	go.preservedSignaled = 0;
+    // tpm-rs differential testing: TPM 2.0 Part 2, TPMA_ACT: "On a TPM Reset or
+    // Restart, preservedSignaled is CLEAR for all ACT. On a TPM Resume, the state
+    // of each ACT signaled is copied to the corresponding preservedSignaled."
+    if(type == SU_RESUME)
+	go.preservedSignaled = go.signaledACT;
     else
-	go.preservedSignaled |= go.signaledACT;
+	go.preservedSignaled = 0;
     
     // For TPM_RESET or TPM_RESTART, the ACTs will all be disabled and the output
     // de-asserted.
